i686 tail call optimization for functions with stack-based arguments (cdecl)
requires argument rearrangement that exceeds peephole pattern matching.
The i686 codegen emits caller-cleanup (addl $N, %esp) and return value
store/reload between the call and epilogue. Converting this to a tail jump
would require semantic understanding of the stack layout to correctly place
arguments for the recursive call — a codegen-level optimization rather than
a peephole transformation.
